! Branch-on-Bit (BB family) acceptance test -- the first program in
! this project to execute the BRANCH ON BIT instruction, which the
! model previously decoded but failed loud on (StretchExecute.bsv
! "tagged BitBranch .*: setOpInvalid").
!
! Encoding source: X22-6533 pocket card "BRANCH ON BIT -- Strap Format:
! OP,B,(I),A(K)" (the eight mnemonics BB/BB1/BBN/BBZ/BZB/BZB1/BZBN/BZBZ)
! and Reference Manual p.41 "Branch on Bit" for the semantics:
!   * the bit at the effective bit address B is tested; if it matches
!     instruction bit 62 (1 for BB*, 0 for BZB*) the branch to A is
!     taken;
!   * then, WHETHER OR NOT the branch was taken, the tested bit is set
!     per instruction bits 60-61: 00 unchanged, 01 zero, 10 invert
!     (negate), 11 one -- so BB=00, BBZ/BZBZ=01, BBN/BZBN=10,
!     BB1/BZB1=11.
!
! Self-checking chain (same mechanism as ibox1_sic_cb_cbz): a single
! word W starts all zeros, and the ONLY path to the PASS halt (BEW,$ at
! label DONE) requires every step below to behave correctly. Any wrong
! result falls into a distinct "BEW,$" HANG whose address names the
! failure. On this model a branch to itself halts (StretchCore.step
! returns True when next==pc), so the testbench PC check distinguishes
! pass (halted at DONE) from fail (halted at a HANG).
!
!   S1 BZB,W,S2   W.0 is 0  -> branch on ZERO bit taken (cond=0)
!   S2 BB,W,HB    W.0 is 0  -> branch on bit NOT taken (cond=1); fall thru
!   S3 BB1,W,HC   W.0 is 0  -> NOT taken, but sets W.0:=1 (modify on a
!                             NON-taken branch -- the key case)
!   S4 BB,W,S5    W.0 is 1  -> taken, proving S3's modify happened
!   S5 BBN,W,S6   W.0 is 1  -> taken (cond=1) and inverts W.0 to 0
!                             (modify on a TAKEN branch)
!   S6 BZB,W,DONE W.0 is 0  -> taken, proving S5's invert happened
!
! Coverage: branch-on-1 vs branch-on-0 (S1/S2/S4/S6), modify-on-not-
! taken (S3->S4), modify-on-taken (S5->S6). Predicted bug injections
! (StretchExecute.bsv's BitBranch arm):
!   A. modify only when the branch is taken: S3 leaves W.0=0, so S4's
!      BB does not branch and the program hangs at HAND (S4's HANG).
!   B. modify only when the branch is NOT taken: S5's invert is skipped,
!      W.0 stays 1, S6's BZB does not branch, hang at HANF.
!   C. never modify: hangs at HAND (S4), same as A's first failure.
!   D. condition inverted (branch when bit != instruction bit 62): S1's
!      BZB does not branch, hang at HANA.
!
! Observed: the unmodified model halts at DONE (PASS PC half-word 3095),
! so every step behaved correctly. Injection A was applied (the modify
! guarded on "tested == modAbc[0]", i.e. modify only when the branch is
! taken) and the model halted at HAND (half-word 3086), the S4 HANG --
! exactly as predicted, and nothing downstream ran to mask it. The
! injection was then reversed by the exact inverse edit (AGENTS.md rule
! 2) and DONE restored. Injections B/C/D are predicted from the same
! reasoning but were not separately run.
!
! Encoding is additionally checked field-by-field by
! verify_bb_encoding.py against the exact bit positions StretchDecode
! reads. That check proves the assembler and the model's decoder agree;
! it does not by itself prove the shared reading of the format is right
! (see AGENTS.md rule 2), so a printed-listing cross-check against a
! real BB line remains an open item (jb_af1c uses BB for sign tests).

        SLC, (8)3000.0
S1      BZB,  W, S2         ! W.0=0: branch on zero bit -> S2
HANA    BEW,  $             ! HANG: BZB failed to branch on a 0 bit
S2      BB,   W, HANB       ! W.0=0: branch-on-1 must NOT be taken
        B,    S3            ! good path
HANB    BEW,  $             ! HANG: BB branched on a 0 bit
S3      BB1,  W, HANC       ! W.0=0: not taken, but sets W.0:=1
        B,    S4            ! good path
HANC    BEW,  $             ! HANG: BB1 branched on a 0 bit
S4      BB,   W, S5         ! W.0 now 1 (S3 modify) -> branch to S5
HAND    BEW,  $             ! HANG: modify-on-not-taken did not happen
S5      BBN,  W, S6         ! W.0=1: taken, inverts W.0 to 0
HANE    BEW,  $             ! HANG: BBN failed to branch on a 1 bit
S6      BZB,  W, DONE       ! W.0 now 0 (S5 invert) -> branch to DONE
HANF    BEW,  $             ! HANG: modify-on-taken (invert) did not happen
DONE    BEW,  $             ! PASS: every BB behaved correctly
W       XW,   0, 0, 0       ! full word of zeros: the bit under test

        END, S1
